              "State transition pipeline"
            ],
            "bug_bounty_scope": "in-scope",
            "notes": "Incorrect version chaining would cause P2P fork digest mismatches."
          },
          "test_procedure": "1. Identify the upgrade_to_fulu state transition function in the beacon node codebase. 2. Examine the implementation to verify that post.fork.previous_version is explicitly set to pre.fork.current_version. 3. Design test cases that exercise the upgrade transition with various pre-states, including edge cases (e.g., genesis fork, consecutive upgrades). 4. Verify the post-condition holds: assert(post.fork.previous_version == pre.fork.current_version). 5. Attempt to falsify by: (a) checking for any code path that could skip the version assignment, (b) testing with corrupted pre-state fork data, (c) verifying no race conditions exist in concurrent state transitions. 6. Validate that fork digest computation downstream correctly uses the maintained version chain.",
          "falsification_strategy": "Attempt to trigger upgrade_to_fulu with edge-case pre-states (empty version, mismatched versions, repeated upgrades) and verify whether the version chain invariant can be violated. Check for off-by-one errors in version array indexing.",
          "bug_class": "State Consistency",
          "risk_category": "Tampering",
          "impact_if_violated": "Fork digest mismatch causing P2P network partition - nodes with broken version chains would compute different fork digests and fail to communicate with correct nodes.",
          "notes": "Source: PROP-W2B3-5, Invariant: fork-SG-002-INV-002, Assumption: asm-009. Bug bounty eligible with PoC showing fork version chain breakage."
